vents{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-04-08T21:25:06Z","updated_at":"2025-04-12T20:22:50Z","closed_at":"2025-04-10T15:20:59Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105164","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105164","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105164.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105164.patch","merged_at":"2025-04-10T15:20:59Z"},"body":"This allows Apple platforms to override the default stack size of a thread in the `WorkerThreadPool`, which is 512KiB by default.\r\n\r\nThis must be increased, as SPIRV-Cross, used by the Metal driver, can use deeply nested stacks. This is exacerbated when using a debug build, which has increased stack-size requirements. Without an option to override the stack size, we have observed stack overflows.\r\n\r\nThe stack size is for Apple platforms is explicitly set to 1 MiB. For `DEV_BUILD` the stack size is set to 2MiB, as debug builds have larger stack requirements.\r\n\r\n> [!IMPORTANT]\r\n>\r\n> `test_rid.h` directly called `std::this_thread::yield()`, so I added a static `yield` function to `Thread`, that can be platform-specific.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"htt